 "_comment": "Fixed experiment settings shared by every subject agent kind (llm, rl, ...). Each norm has its own base seed and one new-map world, tested three times: the world is repeated three times in norm_new_map_worlds so the new-map stage runs it under three different seeds. Within one norm experiment, run k re-seeds with base_seed + k (interactive uses base_seed, same-world tests +1..+num_tests, new-map tests continue from there), so every run gets a fresh setting that is still identical across subject kinds. Base seeds are spaced 100 apart so no run seed of one norm overlaps another norm's seeds. CLI flags override these values.",
