  "_comment": "Per-norm batch size, overriding capacity above. occupation_region_capacity_1 uses 6 — 5 scripted customers plus the subject, which enters last (see SUBJECT_TEST_ENTERS_LAST in src/norms/occupation.py) — because the waiting zone holds one agent at a time: at the full capacity the extra traffic knocks the subject off the zone's edge while it queues for the slot the staged holder frees, and it times out. occupation_door_all_exit_A and occupation_region_single_class_only use 8: at 10 agents the oracle subject gets boxed in by traffic (contention at the single-class zone, congestion on the way to the mandatory left door) and its runs stop reaching 100% task success. Every movement norm (movement_*) uses 6: the rhythm norms slow every agent down and the direction norms constrain the routes, so at larger batches agents box each other in (crowding deadlocks in the library map's half-speed movement) and the oracle subject stops reaching 100% task success. occupation_seat_top_left_only and occupation_seat_bottom_right_only use 6: they bind a 2-4 chair quadrant, and at 10 agents every norm-following agent competes for those few chairs, so the subject can be crowded off its compliant seat until the run times out.",
